  "reason": "Evidence: config_042 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) achieved the best accuracy (0.5988) and F1 (0.5777), clearly outperforming resnet50-based configs (~0.573-0.579) and scgpt (0.494). The fusion method is the one remaining untested dimension within this best-performing architecture: concat slightly beat weighted with resnet50 (0.5793 vs 0.5729), but the interaction with the stronger ViT-L encoder is unknown. This experiment (config_047) is a minimal A/B test—identical to config_042 except fusion=weighted—directly clarifying whether weighted fusion could further improve accuracy with the ViT-L encoder. It is the best use of this slot because it exploits the strongest evidence with a single-variable change, has low expected cost (~4-5 GPU hours, similar to config_042's 4.76), and leaves 4 experiments to explore aggregation (avgpool) or profile setting (singleprofile) if needed."
